  "summary_md": "**Harsh | building Medha ([@ReetuHarsh](https://x.com/ReetuHarsh/status/2115910750573396299))** walks through six security decisions in the Rust **Medha** agent harness: approvals bound to the reviewed file state, shell networking denied by default, compaction that changes the model's view but not the event log, escalation of irreversible actions after web content enters, scanning of skill packages before install, and delegation that intersects child tools with parent capabilities, each linked to code ([tools](https://github.com/kashyaprajharsh/medha-agent/blob/main/crates/tools/src/lib.rs), [sandbox](https://github.com/kashyaprajharsh/medha-agent/blob/main/crates/sandbox/src/exec.rs), [context](https://github.com/kashyaprajharsh/medha-agent/blob/main/crates/context/src/engine.rs), [kernel](https://github.com/kashyaprajharsh/medha-agent/blob/main/crates/kernel/src/loop_.rs), [skills](https://github.com/kashyaprajharsh/medha-agent/blob/main/crates/tools/src/skills.rs), [orchestrator](https://github.com/kashyaprajharsh/medha-agent/blob/main/crates/orchestrator/src/narrow.rs)).",
